---
title: Apply & Verify
---

With your feature flags edited and `AppConfig.swift` regenerated, this step shows you how to rebuild the app in Xcode and confirm your changes in the Simulator.

## Rebuild and Run

Back in Xcode, rebuild and relaunch the app:

{% steps %}

1. Make sure the **VERA** scheme and a Simulator destination are still selected.

2. Press **Cmd+R** (or click the ▶️ Run button) to rebuild and relaunch the app.

{% /steps %}

{% aside type="caution" %}
If Xcode is still showing the previous build, stop the running app first (Cmd+.) before pressing Cmd+R again — otherwise you may see stale behavior.
{% /aside %}

## Verify in the Simulator

Join or start a meeting in the Simulator and check that your changes are reflected. Following the example from the previous step:

{% steps %}

1. Join a meeting room — confirm the initial layout matches your `defaultLayoutMode` setting (for example, a grid layout).

2. Check the in-call toolbar — confirm the screen-share button is hidden if you set `allowScreenShare` to `false`.

3. Try any other flags you changed — for example `allowChat`, `allowCaptions`, or `allowEmojis` — and confirm the corresponding UI element appears or disappears.

{% /steps %}

## Iterating Quickly

A typical configure-test cycle:

{% steps %}

1. Edit `VERA/Config/app-config.json`.

2. Run `python3 ./Scripts/generate-app-config.py`.

3. Run `tuist generate`.

4. Rebuild in Xcode with Cmd+R and verify in the Simulator.

{% /steps %}

Your feature flag configuration is live. Head to the final step for further resources.
